    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-19214",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components",
      "problem": "Let $p=⟨1,-1,1⟩$ and $q=⟨8,4,2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $q$ onto $p.$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{p}\\,q & =\\frac{p\\cdot q}{p\\cdot p}p \\\\  & =\\frac{{p}_{x}{q}_{x}+{p}_{y}{q}_{y}+{p}_{z}{q}_{z}}{{p}_{x}^{2}+{p}_{y}^{2}+{p}_{z}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{1\\cdot 8+(-1)\\cdot 4+1\\cdot 2}{{1}^{2}+(-1)^{2}+{1}^{2}}p \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{3}⟨1,-1,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,-2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
