    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-212459",
      "knowledge_point_id": "84c96375-27d5-5ada-a952-34e09b3e92bf",
      "knowledge_point": "Perpendicular Vectors",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨2,-1,-2⟩$ and $b=⟨x,-4,0⟩.$ Given that the projection of $a$ onto $b$ is the zero vector, find the value of $x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Since $a$ is a nonzero vector, its projection onto another nonzero vector $b$ equals the zero vector only when the vectors are perpendicular. \n\nSo, we must have\n\n$$\na⊥b\\,⟹\\,a\\cdot b=0.\n$$\n\nComputing the dot product, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & ={a}_{x}\\cdot {b}_{x}+{a}_{y}\\cdot {b}_{y}+{a}_{z}\\cdot {b}_{z} \\\\  & =2\\cdot x+(-1)\\cdot (-4)+(-2)\\cdot 0 \\\\  & =2x+4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting the dot product equal to $0,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot b & =0 \\\\ 2x+4 & =0 \\\\ 2x & =-4 \\\\ x & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-2"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "4"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "-4"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "0"
            },
            {
              "type": "math",
              "value": "1"
            }
          ],
          "correct_value": "-2",
          "choices_complete": true,
          "correct_origin": "ma_successful_grade"
        }
      ],
