    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-317652",
      "knowledge_point_id": "c0670172-77cb-5e88-b78d-e5136c06095f",
      "knowledge_point": "Calculating a Vector Projection Using Components",
      "problem": "Let $a=⟨5,-3,4⟩$ and $b=⟨1,2,-2⟩.$ Find the vector projection of $a$ onto $b.$\n\n${\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a=⟨$\n{{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$,$\n{{field-3}}\n$⟩$",
      "worked_solution": "Using the formula for the vector projection, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\text{proj}}_{b}\\,a & =\\frac{a\\cdot b}{b\\cdot b}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{{a}_{x}{b}_{x}+{a}_{y}{b}_{y}+{a}_{z}{b}_{z}}{{b}_{x}^{2}+{b}_{y}^{2}+{b}_{z}^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\cdot 1+(-3)\\cdot 2+4\\cdot (-2)}{{1}^{2}+{2}^{2}+(-2)^{2}}\\,b \\\\  & =\\frac{5-6-8}{1+4+4}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{-9}{9}\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =(-1)\\,⟨1,2,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,-2,2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
